From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Murgola <andy@murgo.la>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:31:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] cuda int8: fuse linear, GELU and convrot quantize

Extends the INT8 linear epilogue matcher to the GELU form of an MLP (linear -> GELU -> ConvRot H256), next to the
existing SwiGLU form. The CUTLASS GEMM writes its F32 result once to the workspace; one kernel then applies GELU
while loading, rotates and quantizes. The separate GELU pass over the F32 activations (a full read and write of
the widest tensor in the block) is gone. Bit-identical output; 488 us -> 329 us per block on an RTX 5090 at
4032 tokens x 8192.
---
 src/core/cuda/int8.cu | 77 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 66 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

